  "body": "## What changed\n\nProcess-only (docs). Three placement rules are added to AGENTS.md, named in the PR-reviewer checklist and the work-issue skill. PROCESS_VERSION 18.\n\nQuoted as added:\n\n**AGENTS.md \"Code shape\"** (two bullets, after \"One concern per subcrate\"):\n\n- **`app` holds the document, nothing else** (maintainer, 2026-11-11: \"high cohesion, low coupling, because every gate is costly\"). New code goes in `crates/app/src` only if it reads or writes the ECS world, the project file, a command, MCP or the CLI. Code that works only on domain values (cl, geometry, tools, post, sim, motion types) goes in the crate that owns them, and `app` re-exports it. A reviewer checks this from the new file's `use` lines: if none names one of those six things, the file is in the wrong crate.\n- **No new dependency between our crates without a decision.** A `camcraft-*` entry added to `[dependencies]` or `[dev-dependencies]` in any `crates/*/Cargo.toml` needs a `docs/decisions/` entry in the same PR. The entry lists the imported items, says why the caller cannot pass the value in instead (a parameter, a closure, a recorded file), and names what now rebuilds when the dependency changes. An edge that would carry fewer than five items is not added: the caller passes the value in. (The wording of the five-item clause is the maintainer's to confirm.)\n\n**AGENTS.md \"Testing\"** (the `crates/app/tests/` line is corrected, then one rule added):\n\n- **A test lives with the code it tests.** A new test file goes in the lowest crate that provides everything it imports, and its Gate map names that crate (`camcraft_post::engine`, not `app::post`). A file in `crates/app/tests/` must import something `crates/app/src` defines; a test that uses only another crate's re-exports (`app::post`, `app::verify`, `app::machining2d`) belongs in that crate's `tests/`. A test that needs another crate's output reads a recorded file (`.cl`, `.cnc`) rather than importing that crate's generator.\n\nAlso: `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md` law check gets a \"Placement\" item naming (a), (b), (c); `.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md` section 2 names the same three rules. `docs/decisions/920-placement-rules.md` records the decision.\n\n## Decision on the fourth rule\n\nThe research proposed a fourth rule (a new test joins an existing suite). It is not in this PR: it waits for directory suites in xtask and for timings (#919 research, Q5).\n\n## Maintainer to confirm\n\nThe \"fewer than five items\" wording of the crate-edge clause is as proposed in the #919 research. Its exact wording is the maintainer's to confirm on this PR.\n\n## How tested\n\nDocs and process only. No code changed, so no test was run for the change. `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --dry-run` plans \"nothing in crates/ changed: no tests to run\". `git diff --stat`: 5 files (AGENTS.md, PR-reviewer.md, work-issue SKILL.md, PROCESS_VERSION, the decision file).\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo review by a second agent yet; the rules' effect on future PR reviews is untested.\n\n## Process\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0 (PROCESS_VERSION 16 at the fork point). PR #963 also bumps PROCESS_VERSION to 17; whichever PR merges second takes 18 when it merges main.\n\nOn merge, announce on #681: `PROCESS_VERSION 18` · PR #<this PR> · AGENTS.md test-placement / crate-dependency / app-scope rules · forks: normal process sync.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #920\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
